insert into public.narrators(id,name,mood,blurb,sample,persona,sort) values
 ('royal-chronicler','Mock-Epic Chronicle','medieval','Solemn King James English; every absurd deed told with total gravity.','Not by accident. Not through illness. But as a calculated demonstration of supreme authority.','Mock-epic chronicle in solemn King James English (thou, thee, hath, -eth), addressing the hero as thou. Every absurd, cowardly or disgusting deed is told with complete epic gravity; the world reacts just as seriously and desperately mistakes idiocy for genius. Short, weighty lines, dramatic build-up and the odd dry aside.',10),
 ('weary-knight','Heroic Saga','medieval','Earnest, sweeping old-fashioned epic, played completely straight.','And the banners of Eldermere rose against the dawn, as they had not risen in a hundred years.','Earnest, sweeping heroic-saga prose in old-fashioned English: honour, oaths, banners and grand deeds, played completely straight.',11),
 ('tavern-bard','Bardic Ballad','medieval','Lyrical and embellished, swelling into rhyme at the big moments.','And lo, the hero strode forth — boldly, nobly, and with his tunic on backwards.','Lyrical, embellished old-fashioned prose (thee, thou, hath) that swells into rhyme at the big moments.',12),
 ('old-chronicler','Old Chronicle','medieval','Dry, formal archaic records, precise and mildly disapproving.','In this year the hero did set fire to the granary. It was not, the chronicle notes, necessary.','Dry, formal archaic chronicle prose, precise and mildly disapproving, recording events as if for posterity.',13),
 ('royal-herald','Royal Decree','medieval','Everything, even trifles, rendered as grand official proclamation.','Upon this day the hero did sneeze, and the whole realm took solemn note.','Pompous archaic prose that renders everything, even trifles, as grand official proclamation.',14),
 ('pirate-captain','Pirate Yarn','pirate','Narration and dialogue in salty pirate English.','The fog rolled in thick as bilge soup, an'' every soul aboard knew the sea was up to somethin''.','The whole story, narration and dialogue, in salty pirate English (ye, yer, arrr, dropped g''s, sea oaths and sea metaphors), boisterous and swaggering.',20),
 ('swashbuckler','Swashbuckler','pirate','Fast, grand high-seas adventure: leaps, blades and booming laughter.','He swung from the rigging with a cutlass in his teeth and a terrible plan in his heart.','Fast, grand swashbuckling high-seas prose: daring leaps, flashing blades, booming laughter and salty dialogue.',21),
 ('pirate-ghost','Ghost Ship Tale','pirate','Eerie sea-ghost story: fog, creaking timbers, omens below.','The fog came in slow an'' polite, and the sea beneath went quiet as a held breath.','Eerie, briny sea-ghost-story prose in old sailor''s English: fog, creaking timbers, omens and things beneath the waves.',22),
 ('pirate-quartermaster','Ship''s Log','pirate','Terse, salty log entries tallying every barrel and insult.','Day nine. Rum: low. Morale: lower. Captain: arguin'' with a seagull again.','Written as terse, salty ship''s log entries, dated, tallying every barrel, insult and broken mast.',23),
 ('sports-commentator','Live Commentary','comedic','Breathless play-by-play, as if it were the final minute of a cup final.','AND HE GOES FOR THE DOOR — UNBELIEVABLE — THE CROWD IS ON ITS FEET!','Written as breathless live play-by-play sports commentary of the action, as if every moment were the final minute of a cup final.',30),
 ('nature-documentary','Nature Documentary','comedic','Hushed and fascinated, observing the heroes like rare animals.','Here, in its natural habitat, the adventurer prepares once again to make a terrible decision.','Hushed, fascinated nature-documentary prose observing the heroes like rare animals in their natural habitat.',31),
 ('campfire','Campfire Horror','atmospheric','Slow dread, long pauses, things just out of sight.','And that''s when they heard it. Right behind them. Breathing.','Creeping campfire-horror prose: slow dread, long pauses, things just out of sight.',40),
 ('noir-detective','Hard-Boiled Noir','atmospheric','Rain, smoke, cynical similes; everyone''s hiding something.','The tavern smelled of cheap ale and expensive lies. She walked in like trouble with a sword.','Hard-boiled noir prose: rain, smoke, cynical similes, short punchy sentences, and everyone is hiding something.',41),
 ('bedtime-grandparent','Fairy Tale','atmospheric','Once upon a time: warm, cozy storybook prose, even when it''s dangerous.','Once upon a time, in a kingdom with far too many dragons, there lived a hero with far too few plans.','Warm, cozy fairy-tale prose, like a storybook (once upon a time), gentle even when things get dangerous.',42),
 ('anime-announcer','Anime Drama','wildcard','Every moment a dramatic turning point; friendship is power.','Could it be?! The power of FRIENDSHIP… has awakened?!','Over-the-top anime prose: every moment a dramatic turning point, shouted declarations, inner monologues and the power of friendship.',50)
